# WF-G178: a GAP REGISTRY is shared coordination state, not a local artifact.
# An orchestrator reads it to pick work and a worker writes the resolve note
# into it, so an ignored registry loses every row on a clean or a reset and no
# other agent sees a row until the file is copied by hand. Git needs the
# directory re-opened before it will look inside it, so each rule below comes
# in a pair: the folder, then the one file kept from it.
!docs/projects/*/
docs/projects/*/*
!docs/projects/*/GAPS.md
!docs/projects/GLOBAL_GAPS.md
# WF-G202: the Spells registry names these living-project pages. Keep its
# two declared targets versioned without reopening unrelated local docs.
!docs/projects/spells/NORTH_STAR.md
!docs/projects/spells/TRACKER.md

# Local-only agent/runtime artifacts from external or desktop-side processes.
.agent/rules/environment-learnings/codex-desktop-terminal.md

# Agora peer-coordination daemon runtime state (snapshot + journal + identity).
# Ignored so a sibling agent's `git reset --hard` cannot nuke live coordination
# state. (Note: `git clean -fdx` would still remove it — see tools/agora/PROTOCOL.md.)
# .agent/ is NOT wholesale-ignored in this repo, so this is path-specific.
.agent/agora/
.agent/agora-*test*/
.agent/orchestration/
.agent/orchestration-*.jsonl

