# img2threejs evaluation artifacts (2026-08-12). The golem's texture maps are
# de-lit CROPS OF THIRD-PARTY REFERENCE ART — published monster illustrations
# and photos of other people's painted minis, held locally under
# .agent/critique-refs/ for comparison only. They must never be published to a
# public repo. The model is served from public/ so the debugger can load it, so
# this rule is what keeps the daily auto-snapshot from committing the pixels.
public/img2threejs-earth/

# Agent worktrees checked out inside the repo. These are git worktrees, not
# submodules, and committing them as gitlinks (mode 160000) made every status
# report them as modified forever.
/Aralia/

# Pane catalog screenshots. Decided 2026-08-28: these stay OUT of git. They are
# a few megabytes per refresh and go stale as soon as a pane changes. The
# catalog shows rows without pictures until someone runs the capture:
#   node scripts/preview/capture-catalog.mjs
public/preview-catalog/

# Untracked 2026-08-29 (Remy's call): 86.1 MB of agent-dashboard art and
# generated test output. The files stay on disk; git just stops carrying them.
# Pet artwork stays local; the small identity catalog is required by Agora in clones.
tools/agora/dashboard/pets/*
!tools/agora/dashboard/pets/pets.json
test-reports/
# One hero-pipeline run's output, 17.5 MB (Remy's call, 2026-08-31). The files
# stay on disk; the plan that names it is status "generated", not "approved",
# so nothing in the game library points at it.
public/creatures3d/hero/fix00000/
# GG-310 (Remy's call, 2026-09-28, before the first nightly save since 08-26):
# the 14 character-atelier race models stay out of git. They are about 270 MB
# of Blender build output, and each rebuild would add as much again to the
# public repo. The builder (scripts/character-atelier/build_characters.py), the
# race recipes and the portraits stay tracked. After a disk loss, download the
# inputs its README names again and rebuild the models in Blender.
public/assets/character-atelier/*.glb

# WF-G141 (Remy, 2026-09-09 sheet q2): the seat roster mirror is runtime state; the daemon rebuilds it from its snapshot on start.
tools/agora/seat-roster.json

